        "second_opinion": null,
        "why": "Both stop() methods run the same graceful-shutdown sequence for an asyncio subprocess: terminate, wait up to 5 seconds, on timeout kill and wait again, log other exceptions, and clear the process reference in finally. A shared helper such as `terminate_process(proc, name, timeout=5)` would own the terminate, wait, kill contract. Legitimate variation stays with the callers: the service name in log messages, the attribute holding the process, and the guard (NEW also checks `returncode is None`, EXISTING only checks that the process is truthy). The callers would keep resetting their own process attribute. The sequence is a coherent process-lifecycle policy, so the overlap is more than similar syntax."
      },
